title: Economic Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: economic_policy_timer <= 0 and dem_president = 1
on-arrival: economic_policy_timer = 6

= Economic Policy

The economy is the foundation of everything. Unemployment stands at [+ unemployed_2 +] percent and inflation at [+ inflation_2 +] percent.

- @stimulus: Stimulus spending
- @investment: Public investment
- @trade_policy: Retool trade policy
- @consolidate: Consolidate and cut deficits
- @easy_discard

@stimulus
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Need 2 budget.
choose-if: budget >= 2
on-arrival: budget -= 2; economic_growth += 1.2; inflation += 0.3; stimulus_level += 1; working_dem += 2*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent -= 3; month_actions += 1

Federal dollars flow. Growth picks up; some economists warn of overheating.

@investment
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; economic_growth += 0.5; unemployed -= 0.2; working_dem += 2*(1-dissent); abundance_strength += 1; month_actions += 1

Roads, grids, and research labs get funding.

@trade_policy
on-arrival: rural_dem += 2*(1-dissent); working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); biz_relation -= 3; intl_relation -= 2; populist_strength += 2; month_actions += 1

We rebalance trade rules toward workers and domestic industry.

@consolidate
on-arrival: budget += 2; economic_growth -= 0.3; biz_relation += 3; progressive_dissent += 4; labor_dissent += 3; month_actions += 1

Fiscal prudence restores room on the books but costs us on the left.
